Add Settings → Admin → Repository variables, and show them in the new-session form.

Admins add a repository, by GitHub repository or clone URL, and give it
NAME=value pairs, typed or pasted as a .env. Values are write-only: the page
lists names, and editing keeps a value whose field is left blank. The page
calls /v1/repo-env (images/server/omnigent_repo_env_api.py, mounted by
0006-repo-env-routes.patch). A repository picked in the new-session form shows
"N variables", which lists the names on click.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0001-0004.

